The engine under benchmark/hubbench/engine/ is a domain-agnostic port of the
FactoryBench-100 engine (https://github.com/blobfishai/factory-agent-simulation,
Apache License 2.0, Copyright (c) 2026 BlobfishAI).  The following pieces were
vendored and adapted:

  - the deterministic, contract-driven verifier (required investigations,
    post-write readbacks, payload assertions, milestone aggregation)
  - the negative-control policy set (noop, shortcut, state_only, incomplete_read,
    write_before_read, missing_readback, unauthorized_write, wrong_value,
    wrong_decision, wrong_evidence), mutation-omission proof, and determinism replay
  - the stdio JSON-RPC MCP server shape (initialize / tools/list / tools/call /
    resources / prompts)
  - the plan / quantity / schedule decision-model bundles (calculation ids that the
    reasoning-chain audit keys on) and the dependency-free XLSX / PDF writers

The ERP-specific world (Oracle Fusion fixtures, Google Workspace and Slack
contracts) was not vendored; HubBench worlds are real SQLite tables behind
provider-shaped tools defined per family.

All HubBench family data is clean-room synthetic.  No real patient, employee,
supplier, or organisation is represented.
